{"id": "EUVD-2025-210056", "enisaUuid": "45b3d7c9-b0d8-33a5-8e01-8e84752645b5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nPCI: endpoint: Add missing NULL check for alloc_workqueue()\n\nalloc_workqueue() can return NULL on memory allocation failure. Without\nproper error checking, this may lead to a NULL pointer dereference when\nqueue_work() is later called with the NULL workqueue pointer in\nepf_ntb_epc_init().\n\nAdd a NULL check immediately after alloc_workqueue() and return -ENOMEM on\nfailure to prevent the driver from loading with an invalid workqueue\npointer.", "datePublished": "2026-06-03T15:49:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:38:44", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/11e78304b0113d3a122dc2c37426adc34c809645", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/829ccfb22950c430f2bf5b40465510c210afb4d5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2f62f8be57882c26f8bede0cab293d013964208f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/314eab6740bcda504ef978be599f805de05ce6de", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/03f336a869b3a3f119d3ae52ac9723739c7fb7b6"], "aliases": ["CVE-2025-71313", "GHSA-q63g-px5v-r7jv"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03e91b63-bcbe-3248-af7f-b163ca02a1e7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "090f619d-bf44-319c-917a-1f9203d65fba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8b821cf761503b80d0bd052f932adfe1bc1a0088 <11e78304b0113d3a122dc2c37426adc34c809645"}, {"id": "182f16f0-2519-3bdb-88ef-4045cba9aee2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "1892cbac-2cb2-32ca-998f-98f3395052ba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "18c688fd-aa73-3536-ae79-7a5375924d60", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8b821cf7